        <briefdescription>
<para>To enable interprocedural analysis, we assign LLVM values to the following groups. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>The register group represents SSA registers, the return group represents the return values of functions, and the memory group represents in-memory values. An LLVM <ref refid="classllvm_1_1_value" kindref="compound">Value</ref> can technically be in more than one group. It&apos;s necessary to distinguish these groups so we can, for example, track a global variable separately from the value stored at its location. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
